{"authored" [{"question" "q-10955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-15}{(x-3)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4e9b988c1f38885c97e4e5d7ff2d5de0d972fbc7ccbe17310ac3eec99db1173" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-15}{(x-3)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\nx-15=A(x+3)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)-15 & =A(-3+3)+B(-3-3) \\\\ -18 & =-6B \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-15 & =A(3+3)+B(3-3) \\\\ -12 & =A(6) \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-2+3=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4e9b988c1f38885c97e4e5d7ff2d5de0d972fbc7ccbe17310ac3eec99db1173" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e2f0edb9809eb216986571ef99ef51b1a93d261b88ea1b5b1e74294deeed33b" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10955" "field